From 6f0c2f5b9c1e4c3a8d7b2e1f0a9c8d7e6f5a4b3c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: freewificam L3 line <l3@freewificam.invalid>
Date: Sun, 26 Oct 2026 18:40:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] rtw89: usb: cap the receive buffer at 8 KiB on the EHCI line

The RTOS EHCI path (CherryUSB host port behind the linuxkpi USB engine)
completes an asynchronous bulk IN of 20 KiB nowhere: the receive URBs never
report data, so a scan table stays empty (rx=0) while the probe requests do
leave the device.  The same driver with an 8 KiB receive buffer receives
beacons and scan results normally, and the platform's native bulk path (the
MSC class, 64 KiB commands) has no such limit - the cut is in the linuxkpi
adapter's asynchronous multi-qTD completion, not in the driver.

This is a platform workaround, not a driver fix: it is applied on the EHCI
line to keep the receive path alive while the adapter/HCD defect is tracked.
A 20 KiB receive buffer remains the upstream value and should be restored when
that defect is fixed.  Frame payloads on the bench (beacons, probe responses,
ARP, ICMP, the raw-L2 data gate) are far below 8 KiB; an A-MSDU larger than the
buffer is dropped in aggregation, not corrupted.

Signed-off-by: freewificam L3 line <l3@freewificam.invalid>
---
 usb.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/usb.h b/usb.h
index 3d1a2b4..9c8e7f1 100644
--- a/usb.h
+++ b/usb.h
@@ -11,7 +11,7 @@
 #define RTW89_USB_VENQT_READ		0xc0
 #define RTW89_USB_VENQT_WRITE		0x40
 
-#define RTW89_USB_RECVBUF_SZ		20480
+#define RTW89_USB_RECVBUF_SZ		8192
 #define RTW89_USB_RXCB_NUM		8
 #define RTW89_USB_RX_SKB_NUM		16
 #define RTW89_USB_MAX_RXQ_LEN		512
